<h2>1. Problem Statement</h2>
<blockquote>
"Rooms are allotted from a paper file. The warden cannot quickly tell which rooms are free in each block. Please build us a system that fixes this."
</blockquote>
<p>
Hostel administration currently manages room allocations using manual paper registers. This legacy approach leads to misplaced student records, slow check-in procedures, and an inability for the hostel warden to quickly determine room availability across different blocks.
</p>
<p>
The objective of this assignment is to build a relational backend system using <strong>Node.js, Express, and SQLite</strong> that stores hostel residents, rooms, and room allotments. The system exposes full CRUD operations and relational queries over a RESTful API, validates all incoming data, and provides search functionality by block and an instant free-rooms check to solve the warden's operational bottleneck. Furthermore, it enforces the custom <strong>Return Flow</strong> twist rule with duplicate return prevention (<code>409 Already returned</code>) and resident allotment history tracking.
</p>

