<h2>10. How to Run the Project</h2>
<p>Install Node.js (version 18 or later) and open a terminal in the project folder <code>hostelhub-booking-system</code>.</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Start the server:</strong>
    <pre>npm start</pre>
    <em>The server runs at <code>http://localhost:3000</code>. The SQLite database file (<code>hostelhub.db</code>) is automatically initialized and seeded.</em>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Run automated tests:</strong>
    <pre>npm test</pre>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Run in Postman:</strong>
    <p>Import <code>HostelHub.postman_collection.json</code> into Postman and execute the collection in Collection Runner against <code>http://localhost:3000</code>.</p>
  </li>
</ol>

<h2>11. Conclusion</h2>
<p>
The <strong>HostelHub Room Allotment API</strong> replaces error-prone paper room tracking with a structured SQLite and Express backend. Residents, rooms, and allotments are stored across three relational tables with foreign-key integrity. Full CRUD operations and block-based filtering are exposed over REST endpoints, and the warden can view free rooms in real-time. Furthermore, the Return Flow twist passes all three required test cases (normal return 200, duplicate return 409 "Already returned", and resident history 200), verified by 15 passing automated test assertions.
</p>

